  "id": "efference-copy",
  "term": "efference copy",
  "definition": "Efference copy is a mechanism involved when a person initiates an action, helping the brain tell apart self-generated sensory events from stimuli coming from outside. In this context, it is discussed together with corollary discharge as part of how responses to self-produced sounds may be reduced or modulated.",
